A plan that satisfies every invariant: `check` is clean, and the other
commands answer from it.

```
$ aplan check
ok: 2 tasks, 0 warning(s), DAG acyclic

```

```
$ aplan ready
A-002  Ship the validator (3d)

```

```
$ aplan why A-002
A-002 is ready: nothing blocks it

```

```
$ aplan graph
graph TD
    A-001(["A-001: Ship the loader"])
    A-002["A-002: Ship the validator"]
    A-001 --> A-002

```

The schema is derived from the Rust types, so pin only its shape here; drift
is caught by `cargo xtask gen-schema --check`, not by a snapshot.

```
$ aplan schema
{
  "$defs": {
...
  "required": [
    "id",
    "title",
    "phase",
    "status"
  ],
  "title": "Task",
  "type": "object"
}

```

`aplan facts` prints the tool's generated facts as JSON. Its contents (the rule,
format, and command lists, and their counts) are pinned by `tests/facts.rs`
against `facts.json`; here we only confirm the command runs and emits an object,
so this case never needs updating when a rule is added.

```
$ aplan facts
{
  "commands": [
...
}

```
